      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1787 Michael Barndollar laid out the town, initially naming it Waynesburg.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Everett%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The borough adopted the name Everett in 1873, honoring Massachusetts orator Edward Everett.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Everett%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Everett sits in a valley where the Raystown Branch of the Juniata River carves The Narrows through Tussey Mountain.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Everett%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Union Hotel and the Bloody Run Historical Society preserve Everett’s historic character with artifacts and exhibits.",
